gine suggested B3. The 14k answered F1, a 24.9-point loss that gave most of it back. Both sides were swinging wildly, but Black stayed well behind."}, {"turn": 45, "text": "B7 lost 28.1 points, the worst move of Opus 5.5's game, dropping from -9.9 to -38.0. The engine's choice was C1. The 14k's A5 on the previous move had lost 28.0 points, so Black had a way back, and B7 did not take it. The last moves barely changed the score, and Opus 5.5 resigned soon after."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints groups with their liberties, count.py only tallies stones and enclosed empty regions for the current position, and the cat/tail and games.md append just read and write notes; none of them chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}